      "question": "I want to know if Transformer 1 at MAIN is running hot compared with its load. Over the available data window, summarize top-oil temperature (oti), its alarm and trip readings (oti_a, oti_t), and the three phase currents (il1, il2, il3) with neutral current (inut), giving min, max and mean for each. Then tell me whether the highest oti reading happened at the same timestamp as the highest total phase current. Flag any phase whose mean current differs from the other phases' average by more than 10%. If oti has no data, use ati for context and say that the thermal correlation can't be confirmed.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (MAIN) \u2014 data window 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19 (5 daily records)**\n\n| Field | Min | Max | Mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| oti (\u00b0C) | 84.0 | 87.0 | 85.4 |\n| oti_a | 1 | 2 | 1.8 |\n| oti_t | 1 | 1 | 1.0 |\n| il1 (A) | 100.0 | 102.0 | 100.6 |\n| il2 (A) | 103.0 | 106.0 | 104.6 |\n| il3 (A) | 94.0 | 96.0 | 95.0 |\n| inut (A) | 5.0 | 6.0 | 5.2 |\n\n**Thermal vs. load correlation:**\n- Highest oti (87 \u00b0C) occurred at **2024-01-16**.\n- Total phase current (il1+il2+il3): 300, **301**, 299, **301**, 300 A. The maximum (301 A) occurred at **2024-01-16 and 2024-01-18 (tied)**.\n- So yes \u2014 the highest oti reading coincides with a highest-total-current timestamp (2024-01-16), though it's a tie with 2024-01-18, and total current varies by less than 1% across the window while oti varies by ~3.6 \u00b0C. The load is essentially flat; the modest temperature swing can't be attributed to load changes.\n\n**Phase imbalance check:** Each phase mean vs. the average of the other two:\n- il1: 100.6 vs 99.8 \u2192 +0.8% \u2014 OK\n- il2: 104.6 vs 97.8 \u2192 +6.9% \u2014 OK (below 10%)\n- il3: 95.0 vs 102.6 \u2192 \u22127.4% \u2014 OK (below 10%)\n\nNo phase exceeds the 10% imbalance threshold, though il2 is persistently the highest and il3 the lowest (~\u00b17%), which matches the small neutral current (5\u20136 A).\n\n**Assessment \u2014 running hot vs. load:** The transformer is running hot in absolute terms regardless of load: oti 84\u201387 \u00b0C with the oil temperature **trip flag (oti_t = 1) asserted at every reading** and the alarm flag mostly at 2. Meanwhile the load is stable at ~95\u2013106 A per phase against a 100 MVA rating. Because both the alarm and trip indications are active continuously while currents barely change, the temperature is not load-driven \u2014 the unit appears genuinely overheated and the oil temperature trip should be investigated (e.g., cooling system, oil condition). Note: with only 5 daily samples and <1% load variation, the thermal-load correlation cannot be strongly confirmed from this window, but the persistent trip flag makes this a hot-running condition.",
      "score": {
